## 4. Modifying State & Handling Events

### Filtering Top-Rated Restaurants

```jsx
<button
  className="filter-btn"
  onClick={() => {
    const filteredList = listOfRestaurants.filter(
      (res) => res.data.avgRating >= 4.5,
    );
    setListOfRestaurants(filteredList);
  }}
>
  Top Rated Restaurants
</button>
```

**Step-by-step flow:**

1. User clicks the button.
2. `filter()` creates a **new** array of matching restaurants.
3. `setListOfRestaurants(filteredList)` is called.
4. React receives the new state, re-invokes the component, and updates the DOM to show only the 4.5+ restaurants.

### Clearing State

```jsx
<button
  className="clear-btn"
  onClick={() => {
    setListOfRestaurants([]);
  }}
>
  Clear All
</button>
```

Passing `[]` into the setter resets the state; the component re-renders and `.map()` iterates zero times, cleanly clearing the screen.

### Resetting to Original Data

```jsx
<button
  className="reset-btn"
  onClick={() => {
    setListOfRestaurants(resList); // resList is the untouched master data
  }}
>
  Reset
</button>
```

> **Key rule:** Never reassign a state variable directly (`listOfRestaurants = ...`). Always call the updater function (`setListOfRestaurants(...)`).

